From 8929d13126d8987a12a0f6da5bc8d975e6b37f2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 02:12:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] MT-FIX1b: engine -- EastSun rulings 20260926: brake
 releases only while the held axes are servo-ON, HT9050 out-of-power predicate
 (G04/G05 open), automatic motor power-on (G31a open)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun rulings 20260926 on the three items MT-E3b left for him:
- G16 "對應軸 Servo On 才放": every golden *BreakerON() release -- CountMotorPowerDelay (G16), DoSystem's idle pass (G05)
  and HOME start (uhome.cpp) -- goes through W906_BrakeReleaseOK(group, site): no hook (ctest) -> golden; otherwise held
  while bMotorPowerState is false (motor power just cut; SnMotorPower lags) or while W906_BrakeServoOnHook says a
  PCI1203 axis of that group is not servo-ON (monitor SVON bit). A held group is released by the next G05 idle pass
  once its drives are ON. Group -> axes on HT9050 (from the IO/Mot table names, to be confirmed on the machine):
  Index -> MTestZ1(/Z2); InOutArmZ -> MInArmZ*/MOutArmZ*; Cassette -> MLoaderZ/MAuto1Z/MAuto2Z; Magazine and
  LDCarRotArmZ have no axis here (outputs disabled/absent). Logged once per group on each change.
- G04/G05: IsIndexMotorOutOfPower() on a PCI1203 Index row (R2) = IsEMGPressed() || SnMotorPower off (golden's Galil
  servo LEDs are never written here, so golden's test was true forever); any other Index config keeps golden's test.
  G04 (golden :4279-4294) and G05 (:4303-4313) opened; G34 iEMGPressDelay defined (golden :133) and its tick opened;
  G15's iEMGPressDelay=8 opened (InitCarlibrationTask still has no port, stays gated).
- G31a: golden automatic motor power-on ~100 DoSystem passes after start-up, opened verbatim (its brake hazard is
  covered by the servo-ON guard above).
- Test containment: TArm::ReadFile/WriteFile (cSocket.cpp) wrote D:\HT9045\system\<Name>.dat / _backup.dat / .ini
  from ctest -- measured 20260926: ctest Automation (Part21 LotInfo_REQUEST -> fLotInfo SaveLotInfo :5308-5311,
  opened by the laptop's W906-LOT-W1 20260919) rewrote ArmByLot0/1/2.dat + _backup.dat. Paths now go through
  W906_MachineRecordRedirect (golden literal byte for byte when W906_MACHINERECORD_DIR is unset = wb_serve/F5;
  every ctest has it set). Per EastSun 20260926 the six machine files are NOT restored.
Tests: MT_E3b_Engine 79/0 (new PART H: guard with/without hook, power-off hold, both predicate arms, G16 releases only
the allowed groups); mainproc_guard fixture now models a powered machine (Index servo LEDs on) -- with G04 open an
unpowered fixture sets iHome=1 through golden's out-of-power lock, which says nothing about the SystemStart guard it
tests; W6_6_Hub, W6_6_CSystemCycle, homeclass, WB_SimPump, WB_State, MachineMotors_HT9050, WebMotorAccess pass;
production_audit 0 changes. Not yet run on the machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
